    {
      "$comment": "P1 player heads: the modular outfits ship their own body geometry (bodyCut keeps head+neck of the fused base; the seam hides in every collar). The pack's Godot-UE export references two textures that do not exist (typo'd `_png.png` names) and defaults to the Dark basecolor variants \u2014 the runtime skin-tint model multiplies DOWN from the Light variants (packages/shared appearance.ts), so both are overridden. `null` drops the broken slot.",
      "pack": "quaternius-base-characters",
      "category": "characters",
      "glob": "Base Characters/Godot - UE/Superhero_*_FullBody.gltf",
      "skinned": true,
      "bodyCut": {
        "meshPattern": "Superhero|Retopology",
        "bones": ["Head", "neck_01"],
        "threshold": 0.4
      },
      "imageOverrides": {
        "T_Hair_1_Normal_png.png": null,
        "T_Eye_Normal_png.png": null,
        "T_Superhero_Male_Dark.png": "../Textures/T_Superhero_Male_Ligh.png",
        "T_Superhero_Female_Dark_BaseColor.png": "../Textures/T_Superhero_Female_Light_BaseColor.png",
        "T_Hair_1_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        },
        "T_Hair_2_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Hairstyles + beard, skinned to the shared 65-bone rig (head bone variant). Eyebrows_* are deliberately excluded \u2014 the base bodies ship eyebrows built in. Hair basecolors bake to a brightness-normalized luminance map (grayscale mean 0.56 \u00d7 1.47 \u2248 0.82) so runtime multiply tints land on the picked swatch with strand shading intact.",
      "pack": "quaternius-base-characters",
      "category": "characters",
      "glob": "Hairstyles/Rigged to Head Bone/glTF (Godot -Unreal)/Hair_*.gltf",
      "skinned": true,
      "imageOverrides": {
        "T_Hair_1_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        },
        "T_Hair_2_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Outfits are full bodies below the neck, incl. their own exposed-skin geometry (MI_Regular_* materials). The pack only ships the Dark skin variant; multiplyRGB lifts it to the Light superhero tone the faces use (per-channel light/dark means measured with sharp), so one runtime skin tint lands on the same color for face and hands.",
      "pack": "quaternius-outfits-fantasy",
      "category": "characters",
      "glob": "Exports/glTF (Godot-Unreal)/Outfits/*_*.gltf",
      "skinned": true,
      "imageOverrides": {
        "T_Regular_Male_Dark_BaseColor.png": {
          "multiplyRGB": [1.062, 1.094, 1.13]
        },
        "T_Regular_Female_Dark_BaseColor.png": {
          "multiplyRGB": [1.036, 1.055, 1.078]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Animation library \u2014 only the clips a shipped phase uses are kept (menus: class poses; world: locomotion; P4: dodge, hit reacts, deaths, spell bolt; P7: level-up Celebration).",
      "pack": "quaternius-ual1",
      "category": "characters",
      "glob": "Unreal-Godot/UAL1.glb",
      "animationsOnly": true,
      "animationKeep": [
        "Idle_Loop",
        "Idle_LookAround_Loop",
        "Sword_Idle",
        "Spell_Simple_Idle_Loop",
        "Spell_Double_Idle_Loop",
        "Spell_Simple_Enter",
        "Spell_Simple_Exit",
        "Spell_Double_Enter",
        "Spell_Double_Shoot_Loop",
        "Walk_Loop",
        "Jog_Fwd_Loop",
        "Jog_Bwd_Loop",
        "Jog_Left_Loop",
        "Jog_Right_Loop",
        "Jog_Fwd_L_Loop",
        "Jog_Fwd_R_Loop",
        "Jog_Bwd_L_Loop",
        "Jog_Bwd_R_Loop",
        "Jog_Fwd_LeanL_Loop",
        "Jog_Fwd_LeanR_Loop",
        "Sprint_Loop",
        "Jump_Start",
        "Jump_Loop",
        "Jump_Land",
        "Swim_Idle_Loop",
        "Swim_Fwd_Loop",
        "Roll",
        "Death01",
        "Hit_Chest",
        "Hit_Head",
        "Hit_Stomach",
        "Hit_Shoulder_L",
        "Hit_Shoulder_R",
        "Spell_Simple_Shoot",
        "Sword_Attack",
        "Sword_Attack_Standing",
        "Sword_Enter",
        "Counter_Angry",
        "Celebration"
      ]
    },
    {
